  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be two finite sets with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> elements respectively. The total number of subsets of the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>56</mn></math> more than the total number of subsets of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. Then the distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
